Consequences, apply them:

- Never use `text-muted-foreground/60` or any text opacity below the full muted colour. The hero trust line (`muted-foreground/60`, 3.11:1) becomes plain `text-muted-foreground`.
- In the glass section no text is dimmer than white at 0.55 (see "Overrides to Appendix B").
- The footer legal line uses white at 0.6 and 12px (Appendix C writes 0.52 and 9px).
- Form controls use `border: 1px solid hsl(var(--field-border))` (3:1 against their background is required for the control boundary); hover `hsl(0 0% 60%)`; focus the green ring.
- Focus is always visible: `:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid hsl(var(--ring)); outline-offset: 3px; }` for every link, button, input and the product viewer. Never `outline: none` without a replacement.
- Green on white or white on green is forbidden; green text sits on charcoal or black only, black text sits on green only.

**Stacking order (z-index):** page 0, hero scrims 1, hero content 10, footer 10, navbar 50, menu sheet overlay and content 60, skip link 70. The footer's `z-index: 100` in Appendix C becomes 10, otherwise it would paint over the menu sheet.

**Reduced motion:** the Appendix A classes start at `opacity-0` and rely on an animation. Add this to the global CSS so nobody is left with invisible text:

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .animate-fade-up, .animate-fade-in { animation: none !important; opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; filter: none !important; }
  *, *::before, *::after { scroll-behavior: auto !important; }
}
```

The footer dots (`footerDotsMove`), the 404 radar sweep and the product viewer's auto-rotation also stop under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.

## Fonts

`index.html` loads, with `display=swap`:

```html
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Sora:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=Inter:wght@300..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
```

- `--font-sora: "Sora", "Inter", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;` and `body { @apply font-sora antialiased; }`. **Sora has no Cyrillic**, so every Mongolian glyph falls back to Inter automatically. That is intended: do not add a third font.
- The glass section uses `"Inter", "Sora", sans-serif` (Appendix B names Inter).
- Appendix C asks for Geist: use the Sora stack instead (Geist is not loaded). Its weights become: the footer H2 `font-weight: 300` (Sora's lightest; the source's 220 does not exist), the wordmark and the brand mark text `700` (Sora's heaviest; the source's 760 does not exist), nav links `600`.
- Mongolian text: `[lang="mn"]` reduces negative tracking. Any `tracking-tight` or `-0.05em` heading gets `letter-spacing: -0.02em` in Mongolian, because Inter's Cyrillic glyphs are wider than Sora's Latin ones and tight tracking makes letters touch. The uppercase wordmark "SENTINEL AI" is Latin and keeps its tracking.
- Before the glass section draws its canvas text, wait for the font: `await document.fonts.load('500 16px Inter', 'Өө Үү абв')` and `await document.fonts.load('500 16px Inter', 'Security')`, then draw. Without it the canvas would use a system font for Cyrillic.

## Language switching (EN / MN)

- Default language is **Mongolian**. Remember the choice in `localStorage` under `sentinel.lang` (always inside try/catch) and honour `?lang=en|mn`. Update `<html lang>` and `document.title` on every switch.
- `index.html` has this inline script in `<head>`, before any CSS, so the first paint already has the right `lang` (and `[lang="mn"]` rules apply immediately). The static `<html lang="mn">` is the default.

```html
<script>
  (function () {
    var lang = 'mn';
    try {
      var query = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('lang');
      var saved = null;
      try { saved = localStorage.getItem('sentinel.lang'); } catch (e) {}
      lang = query === 'en' || query === 'mn' ? query : saved === 'en' || saved === 'mn' ? saved : 'mn';
    } catch (e) {}
    document.documentElement.lang = lang;
  })();
</script>
```

- `LocaleProvider` exposes `{ locale, t, setLocale }`. `t` is the typed message object of the active language (`t.hero.sub`). Switching is instant and **does not reload the page, change the route, restart the Spline scene, reset the 3D product, or move the glass shards**; the glass section redraws its printed text in place (see Appendix B overrides).
- Messages live in `src/i18n/en.ts`, `mn.ts`, `pages.en.ts`, `pages.mn.ts`. `en` is the source of the type: `type Messages = DeepStrings<typeof en>` with `type DeepStrings<T> = T extends string ? string : T extends readonly (infer U)[] ? DeepStrings<U>[] : { [K in keyof T]: DeepStrings<T[K]> }`, and `mn` is declared `: Messages`, so a missing key is a compile error.
- `npm run check:i18n` (imports the `.ts` files directly) flattens both trees (arrays by index) and fails when: key sets differ; a Mongolian value contains no Cyrillic letter (allowed: values that contain no letters at all once `{placeholders}`, digits, punctuation, `©`, the brand `SENTINEL AI` and product codes are removed, such as `12`, `24/7` or `© {year} SENTINEL AI`; and URLs and e-mail addresses); a value is `""`; a Mongolian value has more than 2.2 times the characters of its English value and is longer than 60 characters (a sign that it was not translated concisely); or a `{placeholder}` exists in one language and not the other.
- Brand name, product names and codes (`Sentinel Eye SE-4`, `Sentinel Gate SG-2`, `Sentinel Core SC-8`; they live in `src/content/products.ts`, not in the i18n files) and the phone number are never translated. The names of the two languages on the toggle (`English`, `Монгол`) are fixed constants in `LanguageToggle`, because a language is always named in itself.
- Lists that run in parallel with a constant list (`SERVICES`, `PRODUCT_SLUGS`) are arrays in the same order as that constant; list entries never carry a `key` field. The machine keys (`surveillance`, `camera`, `general`) appear only as property names in `form.topics`, `form.services` and `form.siteTypes`.

## Mongolian must never break the layout (most important rule)

Mongolian strings are usually 20 to 40 percent longer than English, use Ө ө Ү ү, and uppercase Cyrillic with wide tracking is much wider than uppercase Latin. For every text element:

- No fixed widths on text. Use `min-w-0`, `max-w-*` and `clamp()`. Single-line labels get `whitespace-nowrap` plus `truncate` and a `title`; running text wraps with `overflow-wrap: anywhere`. Headings use `text-wrap: balance`. Never `overflow: hidden` on a heading.
- In Mongolian, every uppercase label with tracking of `.1em` or more uses `.06em` (`[lang="mn"]`), and navbar labels are 13px.
- **Navbar:** measured in Sora/Inter, the six labels plus gaps need 563px in English and 642px in Mongolian (13px, uppercase, `.1em` / `.06em`, `gap-6`). With the logo, toggle, button and `px-16` padding the desktop row needs 1,200px, so the desktop navbar starts at **1280px** (`--breakpoint-nav: 80rem`, utility `nav:`), not at Tailwind's `md`. Below it the hamburger shows. At 1280px the row must not wrap or overflow in either language.
- **Buttons** are `whitespace-nowrap` with horizontal padding, never a fixed width. The hero buttons wrap onto two lines of buttons (`flex-wrap`), not inside a button.
- **Cards:** the grid uses `grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,17rem),1fr))]`; card titles may wrap to three lines; no `line-clamp` on body text. Specs and tags wrap (`flex-wrap`).
- **Hero heading:** "SENTINEL AI" may wrap to two lines on a 320px phone ("SENTINEL" / "AI"); that is accepted.
- **Glass section and footer:** see their own sections; both were measured against Mongolian.
- Verify, in **both languages**, at 320, 360, 390, 414, 600, 768, 820, 1024, 1100, 1279, 1280, 1440 and 1920 px wide, and at 1366 × 620, 1366 × 700 and 1440 × 900: no horizontal scroll, no clipped or overlapping text, no button text outside its button, and on every page. Fix the cause in CSS, not by shrinking fonts below the sizes in this prompt.

## Shared shell (around every page)

`ShellLayout` renders, in this order: `SkipLink`, `Navbar`, `<main id="main" tabIndex={-1} className="focus:outline-none">`, `SiteFooter`. The page background is `bg-hero-bg`.

### Skip link, route changes and document meta

- `SkipLink` is the first focusable element: "Skip to content" (`#main`), visually hidden until focused, then a green pill at the top left (`z-70`).
- `ScrollAndFocus`: when `pathname` changes, scroll to the top (or to the element named by `location.hash`, if it exists after render), then move focus to `#main` with `preventScroll: true`. Do not do this on the first load, and do not do it when the path moves between `/products` and `/products/:slug` (the viewer must not jump).
- `useDocumentMeta(titleKey, descriptionKey?)` sets `document.title` (`"<page> | SENTINEL AI"`; the home page uses `t.meta.titleHome`), the meta description, and removes anything it added on unmount. The 404 page adds `<meta name="robots" content="noindex">`.

### Navbar (Appendix A, with these overrides)

- Same structure and classes as Appendix A: fixed, transparent over the hero, `px-8 lg:px-16 py-5`, logo text "SENTINEL" (`text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight`, a link to `/` with `aria-label="SENTINEL AI, home"`), centre links, right-hand button.
- **Links (six):** Services, Products, Projects, About Us, Team, Contacts. Style from Appendix A (`text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground uppercase transition-colors`) with `text-[13px]` and `tracking-[0.1em]` (`[lang="mn"]`: `0.06em`), `gap-6`. They are `<NavLink>`s inside `<nav aria-label>`. The current page's link is `text-foreground` with a 2px green underline (`underline decoration-primary decoration-2 underline-offset-[10px]`) and `aria-current="page"`. Each link is at least 44px tall (`inline-flex min-h-11 items-center`).
- **Breakpoint:** the links, the toggle and the button show from **1280px** (`nav:`), see "Mongolian must never break the layout". Below it they hide, and the hamburger shows. Appendix A's "no hamburger menu on mobile" is overridden, because six links and a language switch cannot disappear on a phone.
- **Right side, desktop:** `LanguageToggle` then the "Get Quote" button (`navCta` variant from Appendix A, `rounded-lg uppercase text-xs tracking-widest px-6`, a link to `/quote`), `gap-3`. The toggle is immediately to the left of the button.
- **Right side, below 1280px:** `LanguageToggle` then a 44 × 44px menu button (`Menu` icon, `aria-label`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls="mobile-menu"`), `gap-2`. The button has the same look as `navCta` (`bg-nav-button`).
- **Scroll state:** at `scrollY > 8` the bar gets `bg-hero-bg/85 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-border/60` (transition 200ms). At the top it stays transparent as in Appendix A. Over the hero, a top scrim keeps the links readable on any frame of the 3D scene: a `before:` layer `absolute inset-x-0 top-0 -z-10 h-[120px] bg-gradient-to-b from-black/60 to-transparent pointer-events-none`, removed when the bar has a background.

### `LanguageToggle`

- A pill with two buttons "EN" and "MN" inside `role="group"` with an `aria-label`. Each button: `lang="en"` / `lang="mn"`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-label="English"` / `"Монгол"`, text `text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest`. Visible pill height 32px; the hit area of each button is extended to 44px with an `::after` (`inset-y-[-6px]`), so the bar does not grow.
