## Glass section on the home page

The Facet design is kept as one full-screen section (`<section id="glass" aria-labelledby="glass-title" class="relative h-[100svh] min-h-[600px] overflow-hidden bg-glass-bg">`). It has two modes:

- **WebGL mode** (`GlassStage`): Appendix B built as specified, with the overrides below.
- **Static mode** (`StaticGlass`): everything else.

**Mode rule** (`useGlassMode`, evaluated on mount and on `change` of the media queries): WebGL only when **all** of these hold: viewport at least 900px wide; `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`; not `prefers-reduced-motion`; not a weak device (the same test as the Spline gate); a WebGL context can be created (`lib/webgl.ts` tries `canvas.getContext('webgl2') || canvas.getContext('webgl')` once and caches the result); and the engine has not reported a failure. Everything else gets static mode. Phones and tablets with a touch screen therefore get the static version; do not try to run the shatter on touch.

