#### The 3D viewer (`ProductViewer`)

- Frame: `relative aspect-[4/3] min-h-[320px] max-h-[70svh] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border` with the background `radial-gradient(circle at 50% 40%, #202020, #141414)`. Under it a caption row: "Drag to rotate" on the left and "Illustrative model" on the right (`text-sm text-muted-foreground`; the second is always shown, because the models are stand-ins for the real products).
- **Renderer:** `WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true, alpha: true })`, `setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2))` (re-read on `resize`), sRGB output, `NeutralToneMapping`, `RoomEnvironment` through PMREM as `scene.environment` (`environmentIntensity` .9), one soft directional key light, `maxAnisotropy` on base-colour maps. Camera fov 30°.
- **Model fitting:** each model (loaded or procedural) is centred and scaled to a bounding sphere of radius 1; the camera distance is `1 / sin(fov / 2) / 0.72`, so every product fills the same share of the frame. No pixel or unit sizes of a particular file appear anywhere in code, so a better GLB can replace a file with no code change.
- **Orbit rig** (own small implementation, not `OrbitControls`): azimuth and polar angles, pointer drag with pointer capture, inertia (damping .92 per frame at 60 fps, frame-rate independent), polar clamp from 25° to 115° from the top, no zoom, no pan, auto-rotate at 0.35 rad/s until the first interaction (and never under `prefers-reduced-motion`; then the loop renders only after an interaction). Set `touch-action: pan-y` on the canvas so a vertical swipe scrolls the page and a horizontal drag rotates. The wheel is never captured.
- **Keyboard and screen readers:** the canvas has `tabIndex={0}`, `role="img"` and `aria-label` = `"3D model of {name}. Use the arrow keys to rotate."`; arrow keys rotate by 0.15 rad per press; focus ring as in "Tokens".
- **Switching products** inside the same viewer: abort the previous load (`AbortController`), ignore any result that belongs to an older request (a request counter), fade the old model out and the new one in over 300ms (none under reduced motion), and dispose the old geometries, materials and textures.
- **Loading** (`loadModel.ts`): `fetch(model, { signal })`, read the body stream to report progress (the text `Preparing the 3D model… 42%` in a `role="status"` line over the frame), parse with `GLTFLoader` (Meshopt decoder and Draco decoder as in "Stack"). If the file is missing, answers `404`, returns `text/html`, or fails to parse, **silently use the procedural model for that slug** (no console output, no error box). A stalled download (no progress for 20 seconds) is aborted and also falls back. Untextured meshes in a loaded model get `MeshStandardMaterial({ color: '#2B2B2B', roughness: 0.5, metalness: 0.25 })`, and meshes whose name matches `/led|light|status/i` get a green emissive `#05E901` material, so a plain free model still matches the palette.
- **Procedural models** (`fallbackModels.ts`), all `MeshStandardMaterial` in charcoal (`#2B2B2B`, roughness .45, metalness .3) with green emissive `#05E901` details (LED, lens ring):
  - `camera`: a cylinder body (radius .32, length 1.1) with a sun shield, a black lens ring and a green inner ring, a short wall arm and plate.
  - `reader`: a `RoundedBoxGeometry` 0.9 × 1.5 × 0.25, a 3 × 4 grid of small key boxes, a green status bar at the top.
  - `hub`: a flat box 2.0 × 0.3 × 1.0 with eight dark port insets on the front, a row of small green LEDs and two rack ears.
- **States:** `idle`, `loading`, `ready`, `gated`, `unavailable`. `gated` (weak device, see the Spline gate) and `unavailable` (no WebGL, or the engine failed) show the product's `ProductIllustration` centred in the frame; `gated` also shows a "Load 3D view" button (44px tall) that starts loading.
- **Lifecycle:** StrictMode-safe (fresh canvas per mount, `cancelled` flag around the async start, no `forceContextLoss()`), dynamic `import('three')` when the viewer is within one viewport of the screen, the loop paused while the frame is off screen or `document.hidden`, everything disposed on unmount, `webglcontextlost` leads to `unavailable`, and `webglcontextrestored` rebuilds once.
- **`ProductIllustration`:** three original inline SVGs (`viewBox="0 0 240 160"`, `fill="none"`, `stroke="currentColor"`, 1.5px, green accents `hsl(var(--primary))`): a bullet camera on a wall arm with a green lens ring; a rounded reader plate with a keypad grid and a green bar; a flat network switch with eight ports and four green dots. They are `aria-hidden`; the card's text carries the meaning.
