### `/contact` and `/quote`

Two forms, one shared look. The contact page is two columns on desktop: the form left, the details right (address, phone as a `tel:` link, e-mail only when configured, opening hours, and "We reply within one working day."). The quote page is a single centred column (`max-w-3xl`).

**Shared behaviour** (`useFormSubmit`, `Field`):

- The client validates with the **same zod schemas** the server uses (`shared/schemas.js`); the schema messages are codes (`required`, `tooLong`, `email`, `phone`, `invalid`, `consent`) that map to `t.form.errors.*`. Validate on submit, then on blur once a submit has been tried. The first invalid field gets focus.
- Every control has a visible `<label>` bound with `htmlFor`; required fields show `*` and are announced (`aria-required`); an invalid field has `aria-invalid="true"` and `aria-describedby` pointing to its message (`text-destructive text-sm`, never colour alone: the message text is always present).
- `requestId` is `crypto.randomUUID()` (fallback: a random hex string), generated once per form fill and **kept when a submit fails and is retried**, so the server can ignore duplicates. A new id is generated after a success.
- Submit: the button is disabled and shows a spinner while pending; a 15-second timeout through `AbortController`; one request at a time. Responses: `201`/`200 ok` leads to a success panel (`role="status"`, focus moved to its heading, a "Send another" button); `400` with `fields` marks those fields; `429` shows `t.form.rateLimited`; `503` shows `t.form.unavailable`; a network error shows `t.form.network`. The status text sits in an `aria-live="polite"` region (errors: `role="alert"`).
- **Honeypot:** an input `name="website"`, `tabIndex={-1}`, `autoComplete="off"`, inside a wrapper `aria-hidden="true"` positioned off screen (not `display:none`).
- Native `<select>` elements (robust with every Mongolian keyboard), styled like `Input`: `h-12 w-full rounded-md border bg-hero-bg px-4 text-base`, border `hsl(var(--field-border))`, hover `hsl(0 0% 60%)`, focus ring green. Inputs are 16px text (no iOS zoom), 48px tall. Placeholders are `text-muted-foreground`.
- The consent checkbox sits in a row with its text; the text links to `/legal/privacy`. The checkbox hit area is 44px.

**Contact form fields:** full name\*, e-mail\*, phone (optional), topic\* (`general`, `call`, `support`, `careers`, `press`; `?topic=` pre-selects, default `general`), message\* (rows 6), consent\*.

**Quote form fields:** full name\*, company, e-mail\*, phone\*, service\* (`surveillance`, `access`, `network`, `audit`; `?service=`), type of site\* (`office`, `retail`, `warehouse`, `residential`, `industrial`, `other`), product of interest (optional: "No preference" or one of the three; `?product=`), preferred contact\* (radio: phone or e-mail, default phone), details\* (rows 6), consent\*.

