## Themed 404 (`*`)

A real, designed page, not a text apology. It is the `NotFoundPage`, shown for every unknown path, unknown product slug and unknown legal slug, inside the normal shell (navbar and footer stay).

- **Words:** eyebrow `ERROR 404 · SIGNAL LOST`; `h1` **`Outside the perimeter.`** (MN **`Хамгаалалтын хүрээнээс гадуур.`**); a sentence ("The page you asked for is not inside our protected area. It may have moved, or the address may be wrong."); the requested path in a line `Requested: /the/path` (monospace system font, `text-muted-foreground`, the path is text only, never HTML, cut to 80 characters with an ellipsis and a `title` with the full value); two buttons ("Back to home" green, "Contact us" `heroOutline`); and a row of quick links (Services, Products, Projects, Contact).
- **Look:** `relative isolate min-h-[100svh] overflow-hidden bg-hero-bg pt-32 pb-20`, content left on desktop, centred on phones. Behind it, `aria-hidden`: a **radar**, `min(90vw, 720px)` square, right-aligned on desktop and centred behind the text on phones at 60% opacity: three concentric rings (`radial-gradient` / `repeating-radial-gradient`, 1px `hsl(119 99% 46% / .18)`), two 1px crosshair lines, a **sweep** (`conic-gradient(from 0deg, hsl(119 99% 46% / .28), transparent 40deg)` rotating once every 6s, linear, infinite), and three small green blips that fade in and out at different times. A large decorative "404" (Sora 700, `text-[clamp(6rem,22vw,16rem)] leading-none`, `aria-hidden`) wrapped by four green **corner brackets** (`::before` / `::after` borders) as if a target were locked. Text keeps at least 4.5:1 over every ring.
- **Motion:** the sweep and the blips stop under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` (the radar stays as a static drawing).
- **Behaviour:** sets `document.title` to `404 | SENTINEL AI` (translated), adds `<meta name="robots" content="noindex">` while mounted, and the server answers **status 404** for the same paths (see "Database", section "Behaviour"). It must use the shell's skip link and focus handling like any page.
- **Language:** all strings from i18n (`t.notFound.*`), so the toggle works on this page too.

