## Language files

Four typed files plus the check script. **Use these strings exactly** (they are the finished English and Mongolian copy); do not rewrite, shorten or "improve" them. The English hero, heading and glass strings are the source designs' own words, adapted only where "Overrides" says so.

How they are used:

- `format(text, vars)` in `src/i18n/format.ts` replaces `{year}`, `{phone}` and `{name}`.
- Eyebrow strings (`glass.eyebrow`, `notFound.eyebrow` and every `eyebrow` in the page files) are stored in sentence case and shown in capitals (`uppercase` in CSS; on the glass canvas `toLocaleUpperCase(locale)`), so the same string works in both languages.
- `form.consent` is split into `before`, `link`, `after` so the link to the privacy policy can sit anywhere in the sentence in either language.
- `glass.terms` has five entries, in the order Zero trust, Edge inference, Access control, Audit log, Response time.
- `products.items`, `services.items` follow the order of `PRODUCT_SLUGS` and `SERVICES`; the product's name and code come from `src/content/products.ts`.
- `projects.items[i].figure` is shown large in green, `result` follows it in `text-muted-foreground`.
- `legal.*.sections` are numbered `1.` to `4.` by the page, not in the strings.
