`VITE_*` values are baked into the client at build time, so they must be set before `npm run build`. `.gitignore` lists `node_modules`, `dist`, `data`, `.env`. The server runs on `0.0.0.0` so a preview iframe and a hosting platform can reach it.

### Docs the project must contain

- `docs/DATA.md`: both tables, which fields are personal data (name, e-mail, phone, company, message, details), the retention rule written in the privacy policy (delete contact messages after 24 months and quote requests after 36 months), and how the owner reads submissions (in the Supabase Table Editor; there is no admin page in this phase).
- `docs/CONTENT.md`: the list of placeholders the owner must replace before launch (see "Data and placeholders"), with the file each one lives in, plus a line that the legal texts need a lawyer's review.
- `docs/CREDITS.md`: author, source URL and licence of every 3D model in `public/models/` (empty table with those headers until models are added); a CC BY or CC BY-SA model also needs a visible credit line under the viewer (the viewer shows `credit` from `products.ts` when it is set).
- Not in this phase, to be added later: an admin page for submissions, e-mail notification of new requests (SMTP), a content security policy. The later policy must allow `fonts.googleapis.com`, `fonts.gstatic.com`, `www.gstatic.com` (Draco decoder), `prod.spline.design` and whatever else the Spline runtime requests (check the network tab; it needs `blob:` and WebAssembly), and `blob:` for `img-src` and `worker-src`.

## Robustness rules every 3D piece follows (Spline hero, glass section, product viewer)

1. StrictMode-safe: a fresh canvas per mount, a `cancelled` flag around async work, full cleanup, no `forceContextLoss()`.
2. Every network request has an `AbortController`, and a stall timeout (Spline 25 s, product model 20 s with no progress, glass first frame 8 s).
3. A failure never blanks the page and never shows a raw error: each piece has a designed fallback (static backdrop, static glass, illustration or procedural model).
4. `webglcontextlost` is handled; `webglcontextrestored` rebuilds once.
5. A weak-device gate (save-data, `deviceMemory <= 4`, `hardwareConcurrency <= 2`, reduced motion) with an explicit "Load 3D" button where it applies.
6. Everything pauses when off screen or when `document.hidden`; three.js is loaded only near the viewport.
7. `localStorage` is always wrapped in try/catch.
8. No `console.log` in the shipped code and no console errors on load.

## Acceptance checklist

**Build and code**
1. `npm install` works on a clean clone with no flags; `npm run build`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run check:i18n` all pass; `npm start` serves the built site; `npm run dev` works.
2. No `esbuild` dependency, no Firebase or Supabase SDK, no `any`, no `console.log`, no secrets, no `rejectUnauthorized: false`.

**Languages**
3. Default is Mongolian; the toggle switches instantly without reload, route change, Spline restart, model reset or shard movement; the choice survives a reload; `?lang=en` works; `<html lang>` and the title follow.
4. At every width in "Mongolian must never break the layout", in both languages, on every page: no horizontal scroll, no clipped or overlapping text, the navbar row never wraps at 1280px, no button text outside its button.

**Home**
5. The Spline hero matches Appendix A (type, spacing, animation delays, buttons); text over the scene meets 4.5:1 (sampled); with Spline blocked or slow the static backdrop shows and the page works.
6. The glass section sits under the hero, matches Appendix B in motion and look, uses the green re-theme, and every text in it meets the contrast and size floors. Hover lift, tilt, shatter into the five terms, "← Back" and the fly-in all work; Tab and Escape work; switching language while shattered and while assembled updates the text in place. Below 900px, on touch, under reduced motion or with WebGL blocked, the static version appears and the five terms open in place.
7. Scrolling past and back to the glass section several times creates and disposes the renderer without errors or a growing memory use.

**Footer and shell**
8. The footer matches Appendix C with the listed overrides on every page; the wordmark "SENTINEL AI" is never clipped from 320px to 2560px; contact lines, legal links and the toggle work; with no social URLs the layout is still balanced; no dead links.
9. The skip link, the focus rings, the mobile menu (focus trap, Escape, scroll lock, closes on navigation) and the sticky bar behave as described.

**Pages and 3D**
10. Every route in the table renders in both languages; an unknown path, an unknown product slug and an unknown legal slug render the themed 404 and the server answers status 404 for them.
11. `/products`: with no GLB files present the three procedural models show and rotate; with a GLB in `public/models/` it loads, is normalised to the same size, and the "Illustrative model" caption stays; switching products quickly never shows the wrong model or leaks; drag, keyboard and touch scrolling all work.
